  "Id": 1927,
  "Title": "AKU faculty, students celebrate World Blood Donor Day",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "The event served to educate the community about the importance of donating blood. ",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass2F8731511DED45FEA0291A50A65F6160\"><p>The faculty and students of the Aga Khan University Medical College celebrated World Blood Donor Day here on June 15, 2019. The event was held by the Haematology and Transfusion Medicine section of the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine. The theme for this year\u2019s event was \u201cBy Donating Blood, you can Save Lives,\u201d and was held to educate the community about the importance of donating blood.&#160;<br></p><p>The event served to raise awareness of the need for regular blood donations so that communities have access to affordable timely supply of safe blood.</p><p>\u201cThe real spirit of World Blood Donor day rests with the donors who don\u2019t ask for compensation and donate voluntarily,\u201d said Natasha Ali, Associate&#160;Professor and Section Head Haematology and Transfusion Medicine.&#160;&#160;</p><p>The event was attended by over 200 participants, including chairman Karachi Lions AKUH Blood Bank Committee, Anwar Ajanee, blood bank staff, faculty, residents and students.&#160;</p><p>\u201cThere is a lot of physical and emotional labour that goes in b\u200blood donation but looking at the enthusiasm of donors on this day is very heartwarming and makes one realise that the struggle must continue,\u201d said Sejal Atta Gondal of Falah, AKU\u2019s student organisation.&#160;\u200b</p></div>",
